==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Plug Suit Rei''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Reunion Li'l Rei''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Rei can do well at weakening melee Angels such as [[Heavenly Hippoe]], [[Angelic Gory]], and even [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] (until he lashes out with one too many [[Wave Attack|Waves]], of course) so that [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] can tank them even better. However, [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] already weakens these enemies well and even tops Rei's already good uptime, and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] can multitask with his [[Weaken|Weaken]] [[Talents|Talent]] and covers Thaumaturge's weakness of lacking [[Area Attack]]. Another interesting ability Rei has is [[Immune to Weaken]]. This may have been to counter [[Winged Pigge]] and [[Unit-13's False Evolution]], though both tear her to shreds due to pierce.

Rei is a suitable substitute for [[EVA Angel Killer]] Ubers against EVA Angels early on. It's highly recommended that you use the [[You Will Find Happiness (Combo)|You Will Find Happiness]] [[Cat Combo]] when pitching her against such foes.

==='''True Form'''===
Rei's True Form gains a variety of buffs that make her a very strong unit against Angels. Most notable is Rei's gain of [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] Angels, which increases her effective health to 108,000—with her Weaken, this goes to 216,000. This single-handedly turns Rei from an anti-Angel CC unit to a tank similar to the like of Ramen Cat. Rei's CC capabilities is also enhanced by her higher health—a notable problem, especially in later parts of the game, was that Rei's Weaken ability wouldn't really do much if she died after getting a single hit in. Reunion Li'l Rei's damage is also affected by her Strong ability, giving her an effective 30,294 damage against Angels and 5.3k DPS at level 30. With her increased damage, Rei can now get a damage knockback against high-powered frontline enemies like Angelic Gory and give her more time to live, as well as even working as an anti-Angel attacker. To put her damage into perspective, she deals slightly more damage than [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]], although Rei's lengthy cooldown and lower DPS means that you shouldn't be using her as your main source of anti-Angel damage.

Finally, Rei gains a 20% chance to [[Dodge]] attacks from Angel enemies. Similarly to [[Juvens (Uber Rare Cat)|Juvens]], Reunion Li'l Rei can take advantage of the speed of which Angel enemies like Angelic Gory, [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] attack, and pull off multiple Dodges in short periods of time, greatly improving her survivability.

Overall, Rei's True Form, especially for its very cheap cost, becomes a genuinely good tank against Angel enemies that has enough tools to set her apart from Ramen. Unlike Ramen, her performance in mixed stages is not very good since she relies on abilities to maintain her effective HP; do your best to prevent her from taking unnecessary damage from other enemies.

